S:\nCardSmart\nClass schedule\nHousing portal\nCardinal Careers\nCampus Store\nSee all\nFACULTY & STAFF:\nWorkday\nHuman Resources\nDirectory\nCampus Solutions\nUofL Folio\nSee all\nGraduate School\nApply Now\nRequest Info\nFaculty & Staff Resources\nSite Search\nGraduate School\nAll of UofL\nSearch\nSearch\nClose Search Tray\nAdmissions\nHow to Apply\nWhy UofL?\nPrepare for Graduate School\nConnect with UofL\nInternational Applicants\nAdmitted Students\nAdmission FAQs\nAcademics & Research\nPrograms & Degrees\nResearch\nGraduate Catalog\nGraduate Faculty\nDGS List\nPolicies and Procedures\nMilestones & Degree Completion\nUofL Facts & Figures\nFrequently Asked Questions\nFunding, Tuition & Aid\nTuition & Cost of Attendance\nFunding Opportunities\nFunding Policies\nFunding Questions\nFunded Student Checklist\nGraduate Student Life\nInclusive Excellence\nGraduate Student Groups\nLife in Louisville\nResilience and Wellbeing\nAwards and Recognition\nGraduate Student Resources\nProfessional Development\nWhat's Your PLAN?\nPrograms & Events\nGraduate Teaching Assistants\nMentorCenter\nCareer Development\nProfessional Development Resources\nAbout Us\nMessage from the Dean\nUnits and Offices\nGraduate School Staff\nContact Us\nGraduate News\nGraduate Newsletters\nBreadcrumb\nHome\n.....\nHome\nAdmissions Main\nGraduate International Applicants\nEnglish Language Proficiency\nEnglish Language Proficiency Requirements\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nabout\nInternational Credential Evaluation\nRequirements for International Credential Evaluation\nSidebar\nIn this section\nInternational Applicants\nEnglish Language Proficiency\nInternational Credential Evaluation\nInternational Credential Evaluation Requirements\nTOEFL Score Scale Change: Effective January 21, 2026, TOEFL will implement a new 1.0\u20136.0 score scale. In response, the University of Louisville will require a minimum overall score of 4.0, with minimum sub-scores of 4.0 in each skill area.\nIn addition to other admissions materials, international students whose native language is not English must submit proof of language proficiency. The University of Louisville currently accepts TOEFL, IELTS, DET and PTE Academic.\nScore reports are valid for two years and scores will be considered expired if the test was taken more than two years prior to the application deadline.\nTest\nMinimum Score\nTOEFL\n79 iBT (before January 2026), 4.0 (with 4.0 minimum sub-scores) (after January 2026), 213 cBT, 9.0 (Essentials)\nIELTS\n6.5 (no sub-score lower than 5)\nDuolingo English Test (DET)\n105\nPTE Academic\n55 (no sub-score lower than 53)\nEnglish proficiency requirements are not waived based upon the medium of instruction at a previously attended institution.\nProof of language proficiency is waived for International Students with citizenship from one of the following English-speaking countries:\nCountries and Territories\nAmerican Samoa\nChristmas Island\nGrenada\nLiberia\nNorway\nSt. Lucia\nVirgin Islands\nAnguilla\nCook Islands\nGuam\nMalawi\nPalau\nSt. Vincent and the Grenadines\nWales\nAntigua and Barbuda\nDenmark\nGuyana\nMalta\nPapua New Guinea\nSweden\nZambia\nAustralia\nDominica\nIreland (Northern & Republic of Ireland))\nMarshall Islands\nPitcairn Islands\nTanzania\nZimbabwe\nBahamas\nEngland\nIsle of Man\nMicronesia\nScotland\nThe Gambia\nBarbados\nEswatini (Swaziland)\nJamaica\nMontserrat\nSeychelles\nTonga\nBelize\nFalkland Islands\nKenya\nNamibia\nSierra Leone\nTrinidad and Tobago\nBermuda\nFiji\nKiribati\nNetherlands\nSingapore\nTurks and Caicos Islands\nBotswana\nFinland\nLesotho\nNew Zealand\nSouth Africa\nTuvalu\nCameroon\nGhana\nMarshall Islands\nNigeria\nSouth Sudan\nUganda\nCanada (except Quebec)\nGibraltar\nMicronesia\nNiue\nSt. Helen\nUnited Kingdom\nCayman Islands\nGrand Cayman Islands\nMontserrat\nNorfolk Islands\nSt. Kitts and Nevis\nVanuatu\nStudents holding a bachelor's or advanced degree from an accredited institution in the United States, Canada (except Quebec), the UK and Australia may also be exempt from this requirement.\nBegin your graduate education journey with us!\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nTop\nContact Us\nPhone:\n502-852-6495\nEmail:\ngraduate@louisville.edu\nHours:\nMonday \u2014 Friday\n9 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\nNo holiday hours\nAddress:\nHouchens Bldg., Rm 105\n2211 S. Brook St.\nLouisville, KY 40292\nConnect with Graduate School\nfacebook\ninstagram\nyoutube\nlinkedin\nAdmissions\nAcademics & Research\nFunding, Tuition & Aid\nGraduate Student Life\nProfessional Development\nAbout Us\nSubmit a Story to the Graduate School News\nSubmit to our Newsletters\n\u00a9 2026 University of Louisville\nAccessibility\nAccreditation\nAlerts\nConsumer Information\nPrivacy\nTitle IX", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://graduate.louisville.edu/admission/international/proficiency#main"], ["", "https://louisville.edu"], ["Areas to Support Read more about", "https://give.louisville.edu/s/1157/19/fdn/interior.aspx?sid=1157&gid=1&pgid=2319"], ["Ways to Give Read more about", "https://give.louisville.edu/s/1157/19/fdn/interior.aspx?sid=1157&gid=1&pgid=2336"], ["Blackboard Read more about", "http://blackboard.louisville.edu/"], ["CardBox Read more about", "https://louisville.app.box.com"], ["Email Read more about", "http://outlook.office365.com/"], ["Parking Read more about", "https://louisville.edu/parking/"], ["ITS Helpdesk Read more about", "https://louisville.edu/its/get-help/its-helpdesk"], ["ULink Read more about", "https://ulink.louisville.edu/"], ["CardSmart Read more about", "https://louisville.campus.eab.com/"], ["Class schedule Read more about", "https://courseleafpath.louisville.edu"], ["Housing portal Read more about", "https://louisville.starrezhousing.com/StarRezPortalX/248308C1/1/1/Home-Home?UrlToken=DCE93C36"], ["Cardinal Careers Read more about", "https://cardinalcareers-csm.symplicity.com/"], ["Campus Store Read more about", "https://www.bkstr.com/uoflstore/home"], ["See all Read more about", "https://